  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I verified TX-0401 in account ACC-1005 (EUR):\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Direction:** Outgoing card payment\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nYour records also show **TX-0402**, dated 2026-07-14, for the same amount (EUR 240.00) at the same merchant. You may want to check whether that is related.\n\nBased on the reason codes available, these could apply, depending on what happened:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge**: You were charged more than once for the same purchase. This could fit if TX-0401 and TX-0402 are two charges for one order.\n2. **unauthorized_debit**: You did not make or authorize this payment.\n3. **fraud_card_not_present**: The payment was made using your card details online without your authorization, which may fit if someone obtained your card data.\n4. **goods_not_received**: You paid for something that was never delivered.\n5. **service_not_rendered**: You paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nTell me which situation matches what happened, and I will check whether a dispute can be opened under that code. I have not opened anything. If the payment was unauthorized and you suspect fraud, let me know, since that may need to be handled by a human agent.",
